nly on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:52:# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:53:# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:60:# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:62:bb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:84:change (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:89:and spawned programs that changed (target/yin-repl.js, Dart peers).\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:101:bb test:sub:cljd <subsystem>...   # Dart lane alone\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:103:bb test:sub <subsystem>... --slow # Include slow tests (-i :slow on JVM, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1 on Node/Dart)\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:141:  scenario in process, over the `dao.jing.dht` test mesh seam. Dart's\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:142:  signed-name leg runs here, because no Dart `yin.repl.main` process\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:147:# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:148:clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch <build-id>    # e.g. watch demo\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:149:clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build-id>  # e.g. compile demo\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:150:clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release <build-id>  # production release\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:152:# ClojureDart\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:159:The Dart `bb` lanes run `src/dev/cljd_agg.clj` (`bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:162:Dart file. `--slow-regex` prints those namespaces as an anchored alternation\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:163:with its dots already escaped for an EDN string (bb.edn feeds it to shadow-cljs\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:212:4. **After brackets balance**, rerun `clj-kondo`, then rebuild with `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build>`.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:12:   belongs to the evaluator (phase 4); the static facts of §8.1 are\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:253:;; Item 6: body partition, ownership, and the §3.1 parse\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:258:   ownership is judged: `[{:start s :end e :owner pc-or-nil} …]` in pc\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:260:   body-pc, each body running to the next one's start. `:owner` is the pc\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:263:  (let [owners (reduce (fn [m pc]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:271:        starts (vec (sort (conj (set (keys owners)) 0)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:274:            {:start s, :end e, :owner (when (pos? s) (get owners s))})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:293:  \"Item 6's partition and ownership clauses, in this order: a `:closure`\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:295:   already owns; an owner inside the body it owns; an owner chain that\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:305:                                 (not= pc (:owner (nth bodies\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:310:                (let [owner (:owner (nth bodies i))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:311:                  (when (= i (body-of owner))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:312:                    (tuple-defect :body-partition owner))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:320:                                      (:owner (nth bodies i)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:321:                        :else (recur (body-of (:owner (nth bodies j)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:439:  \"Item 6. Partition and ownership defects are `:body-partition`; a body\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:856:(defn parse\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:858:   :end e :owner closure-pc-or-nil :expr tree :registers k} …]`.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc:868:   `{:vector v :address A :bodies [{:start :end :owner :registers} …]}`,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:21:a specified re-emission (§5.5), the harness matrix is expanded (§5.2),\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:22:6a is the independent codec (§8.1), and the amendment inventory is\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:29:with its owner (§6.3), E2 requires lexical presence and X1 validates the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:32:cross-lane re-emission takes an explicit stream correspondence (§5.5),\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:42:Every section marks its content **DECIDED** (an owner ruling, frozen\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:56:verification honesty · §10 findings and amendments · §11 owner\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:146:- A **reified continuation** is `values/continuation owner (assoc act\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:197:steps 1-6 and 8-12 stand.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:284:  §5.4, §5.5), unchanged.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:286:### 2.6 The root (replacing draft §5.5 in two slots)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:308:   custody]         ; plain, draft §5.5's table\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:312:profiles' (v2 amendment §2, §4.1). The custody table of the draft §5.5\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:317:**PROPOSED.** `rows->frame` and `frame->rows` (`yin.vm.ucf.rows`, §8.1)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:355:(`resolve-name`, for the chain of rule E2) and `yin.vm`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md:369:(`code/parse`); `inst(p) = (nth v p)`; `chain(b