{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,190p' test/yin/vm/ucf/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; sed -n '810,855p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md; rg -n 'numeric-kind|bytes-hex' src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc | head\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.safepoint-harness-test\n  \"D16-prep: the safepoint conformance harness (UCF 7.4.1; 7.11.1's\n   safepoint-reconstruction row and its acceptance blocker; linker-dht\n   14.1.1 and 14.1.3's second row).\n\n   Every corpus segment is run to every liftable row of 7.4.1 -- explicit\n   park, blocked read, blocked write, sent FFI, retained FFI, ordinary and\n   tail effectful calls, halt -- on both fork body versions: version 0\n   (the semantic profile, the only one it speaks) and version 2 (the four\n   profiles).  The corpus wraps each row's parking expression in four\n   segments: bare, as an operand, three ordinary activations deep, and\n   inside a closure called with a captured environment.\n\n   Each case builds the same program twice.  The reference build is\n   satisfied and run on its own machine; the handoff build is lifted to\n   canonical bytes, lowered into a fresh machine over the toy channel,\n   satisfied through the source's streams and run through the\n   reflections.  Result and effect trace must agree; `lift(lower(frame))`\n   must reproduce the lifted body; the frame's reason is the observed\n   wait's.  An explicit park is checked through its parked record: no\n   frame, the record by its own id, the controlled `:vm/resume`.  Halt is\n   a result, not a frame.\n\n   Beside the matrix: one pc reached by two activations of different\n   depth and captured environment, handed off at each; a nonempty ready\n   queue; a kept FFI response cursor shared by two waiters; and a real\n   held immediate (the D4 `:observe` entry), which refuses export.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.handoff :as handoff]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n\n\n(def ^:private lanes\n  \"Every [profile version] pair: version 0 speaks the semantic profile\n   only; version 2 all four.\"\n  (into [[:semantic 0]] (map (fn [e] [e 2])) s/engines))\n\n\n(defn- lift\n  \"The fork lift of `m` at `version` over `peer`'s served table.\"\n  [m version t peer surfaces]\n  (handoff/export-task m (s/server peer (:channel t) surfaces)\n                       (when (= 2 version) {:version 2})))\n\n\n(defn- drive-peers\n  \"Run `m` through its reflections, stepping every peer's mirror between\n   rounds, until it stops blocking.\"\n  [m peers rounds]\n  (loop [m (vm/run m), n rounds]\n    (if (or (not (vm/blocked? m)) (zero? n))\n      m\n      (do (run! s/serve-mirror! peers)\n          (recur (vm/run m) (dec n))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The corpus: four segments around one parking expression\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- with-cat\n  \"`ast` with `cat`, a closure conj-ing its two arguments, in scope.  The\n   corpus combines through it, not through the `conj` primitive: the\n   register profile cannot resume a wait whose live registers hold a\n   host primitive (`:continuation-registers`, reported with D16-prep),\n   and a closure keeps that defect out of every other row's evidence.\"\n  [ast]\n  (s/let1 'cat (s/lam ['p 'q] (s/app (s/v 'conj) (s/v 'p) (s/v 'q))) ast))\n\n\n(defn- cat-of\n  [p q]\n  (s/app (s/v 'cat) p q))\n\n\n(defn- nest\n  \"`op` inside `d` ordinary (non-tail) closure activations.\"\n  [d op]\n  (if (zero? d)\n    op\n    (cat-of (s/lit [d]) (s/app (s/lam ['x] (nest (dec d) op)) (s/lit d)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private corpus\n  \"Each segment binds `cat` around its whole body, so a row's parking\n   expression may combine through it too.\"\n  (mapv\n    (fn [[label seg]] [label (comp with-cat seg)])\n    [[:bare identity]\n     [:operand (fn [op] (cat-of (s/lit [:operand]) op))]\n     [:depth-3 (fn [op] (nest 3 op))]\n     [:captured\n      (fn [op]\n        (s/let1 'k (s/lit :captured)\n                (s/let1 'f (s/lam ['y] (cat-of (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'k))\n                                                       (s/v 'y))\n                                               op))\n                        (s/app (s/v 'f) (s/lit :arg)))))]]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The rows: one builder per 7.4.1 row\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; A builder answers the parked machine and how to satisfy its wait: the\n;; steps run in order, each followed by a drive; `:finish` and the\n;; receiver's own `:finish` record the effect trace into `:trace`.\n\n(defn- read-row\n  \"A blocked read at a kept position: A consumed, B unread.\"\n  [engine seg]\n  (let [m0 (vm/run (s/load-ast\n                     engine (s/new-machine engine)\n                     (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4}\n                             (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's))\n                                     (seg (s/let1 'a (s/next-of (s/v 'c))\n                                                  (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'a))\n                                                          (s/next-of (s/v 'c)))))))))\n        src (s/stream-of m0)]\n    (stream/append! src \"A\")\n    {:machine (vm/run m0)\n     :kind :blocked\n     :reason :next\n     :steps [#(stream/append! src \"B\")]\n     :trace (atom [])}))\n\n\n(defn- write-row\n  \"A blocked write: the one-slot target is warm, the value retained.\"\n  [engine seg]\n  (let [trace (atom [])\n        w (support/one-slot-stream \"w\")\n        _ (stream/append! w :warmed)\n        m0 (s/load-ast engine (s/new-machine engine)\n                       (seg {:type :stream/put, :target (s/v 'w),\n                             :val (s/lit \"v\")}))\n        [ref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n        take! #(swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next w 0)))]\n    {:machine (vm/run (assoc m1 :store {'w ref}))\n     :kind :blocked\n     :reason :put\n     :surfaces #{:reader :writer}\n     :steps [take!]\n     :finish take!\n     :trace trace}))\n\n\n(defn- own-call-pair\n  \"The receiver's own FFI pair: a subsequent call uses it, so the trace\n   records what it carried.\"\n  [trace]\n  (let [own-in (s/ring 8)\n        own-out (s/ring 8)]\n    {:opts {:call-in own-in\n            :call-out own-out\n            :call-out-cursor (vm/mint-oldest own-out :test)}\n     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain own-in))}))\n\n\n(defn- sent-ffi-row\n  \"A sent FFI call awaiting its correlated response.\"\n  [engine seg]\n  (let [trace (atom [])\n        call-in (s/ring 8)\n        call-out (s/ring 8)\n        m (vm/run (s/load-ast engine (s/calling-machine engine call-in call-out)\n                              (seg (s/call-node :op/echo \"hello\"))))\n        id (ffi/response-call-id (first (:wait-set m)))]\n    {:machine m\n     :kind :blocked\n     :reason :ffi\n     :steps [#(stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response id \"echo!\"))]\n     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain call-in))\n     :receiver #(own-call-pair trace)\n     :trace trace}))\n\n\n(defn- retained-ffi-row\n  \"An FFI request retained behind a full call-in; once the slot frees,\n   the retry lands and the response correlates.\"\n  [engine seg]\n  (let [trace (atom [])\n`(f :arg)`). A row's own `let1`s add theirs. Row 20 alone runs outside\nthe wrappers.\n\nPrograms use `v2_support`'s AST helpers (`v2_support.cljc:56-104`:\n`lit v lam app def! then cursor-of next-of let1`) and the four segments\nof the old harness (`safepoint_harness_test.cljc:92-106`: `:bare`,\n`:operand`, `:depth-3`, `:captured`); `cat` is the closure `(fn [p q]\n(conj p q))` bound around every body (`:69-81`). \"Expected\" is the\nreference run's normalised result; where a row says \"executable\" it runs\non all three lanes; \"synthetic\" means the frame is built by hand and\njudged by `frame/defect` only, because no program reaches it on the\nlanded or stage-2 evaluator.\n\n| # | Row | Program (inside each segment) | How parked / satisfied | State, pending | Expected after satisfy | Executable? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | blocked read | `(let1 s (stream/make 4) (let1 c (cursor-of s) (let1 a (next-of c) (cat (cat [] a) (next-of c)))))`, `\"A\"` appended before the run | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next` | `[\"A\" \"B\"]` | yes |\n| 2 | blocked write | `(stream-put w \"v\")` on a one-slot stream warmed with `:warmed` | take one | act, `:put` with retained `\"v\"` | `\"v\"` landed | yes |\n| 3 | FFI sent | `(dao.stream.apply/call :op/echo \"hello\")` | append the success response | act, `:ffi` | `\"echo!\"` | 4b stage 2 |\n| 4 | FFI retained | as 3 with a one-slot, warmed call-in | free the slot, then answer | act, `:ffi-request` | `\"echo!\"` | 4b stage 2 |\n| 5 | effectful call, non-tail, stream | `(cat [:ordinary] (stream/next! c))` | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next` | `[:ordinary \"B\"]` | yes (stage 1 has streams; `stream/next!` is the stream module's) |\n| 6 | **effectful call, tail, stream** | `((fn [u] (stream/next! c)) 0)` with the inner call `:tail? true` | append `\"B\"` | **tail**, `:next` | `\"B\"` delivered through `K` | yes |\n| 7 | link request phase | `(require 'host.mod)` parked **before** the request append succeeds (one-slot, warmed request stream) | free the slot, then answer `:ok` | act, `:link-request` | `'host.mod` | 4b stage 2 |\n| 8 | link response phase | `(require 'host.mod)` polling (request appended) | append the `:ok` response | act, `:link-response` | `'host.mod` | 4b stage 2 |\n| 9 | **link, tail** | `((fn [u] (require 'host.mod)) 0)` tail | as 8 | **tail**, `:link-response` | `'host.mod` through `K` | 4b stage 2 |\n| 10 | install, child running | `(require 'host.mod)` where `host.mod`'s body reads a stream the test has not fed, so the child is `:blocked` and the parent's wait is `:install` | feed the child's stream | act, `:install` + install entry, child kind `:blocked`, phase `:running` | `'host.mod` | 4b stage 2 |\n| 11 | install, child parked | as 10 with the child body executing `:park` | resume the child by id | act, `:install`, child kind `:parked`, phase `:parked` | `'host.mod` | 4b stage 2 |\n| 12 | install, tail | `((fn [u] (require 'host.mod)) 0)` tail with 10's child | as 10 | **tail**, `:install` | `'host.mod` through `K` | 4b stage 2 |\n| 13 | explicit park | `(vm/park)` | `(vm/resume pid \"back\")` beside | parked record, root `:parked` | `\"back\"` | yes |\n| 14 | reified capture live in a window | `(let1 k (vm/current-continuation) (cat (cat [] k) (next-of c)))` | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`; `k` is a `:reified` value in `W` | `[:continuation \"B\"]` normalised | yes |\n| 15 | capture invoked after lower | `(let1 k (vm/current-continuation) (if (= k :second) :done (let1 r (next-of c) (k :second))))`: on the first pass `k` is a continuation, so the test fails and the read runs and parks; after satisfaction `(k :second)` delivers `:second` into the capture's `rd` (the `let1` operand) and re-enters at the capture's successor pc, so the body is entered again with `k = :second` and the test succeeds **without repeating the read** (the invocation is abortive on every lane: `:continuation` operator kind, `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:212-217` stage 2, `stack.cljc:760-763`). `if` is `{:type :if :test :consequent :alternate}` (`vm.cljc:1069`), a helper the new harness file adds; `=` is the primitive (`vm.cljc:387`), consumed before the read | append `\"x\"` after lower | act, `:next`; `k` is a `:reified` value in `E` (the closure's) | `:done` | yes |\n| 16 | nested capture | `(let1 k1 (vm/current-continuation) (let1 k2 (vm/current-continuation) (cat (cat (cat [] k1) k2) (next-of c))))` | append `\"B\"` | act; `k2`'s act window holds `k1` (a `:reified` inside a `:reified`'s window) | `[:continuation :continuation \"B\"]` | yes |\n| 17 | module context, blocked inside a module closure | `host.mod` exports `f = (fn [c] (stream/next! c))`; root: `(f c)` after `(require 'host.mod)` | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`, `E` carries `store-of host.mod` | `\"B\"` | 4b stage 2 (link) |\n| 18 | module-store snapshot | `parked-module-store-cursors` (`lift_support.cljc:310-333`): an explicit park whose module store holds two cursors named by a module closure | resume | parked record; `:module-store` row | the cursors' cells | yes |\n| 19 | halt | `(lit 42)` | — | result | `42` | yes |\n| 20 | **tail-effect halt** | run **outside the wrappers**, in two batches on one machine: a setup batch `(then (def! 's (stream/make 4)) (def! 'c (cursor-of s)))` run to halt (store writes persist across batches, as `lift_support.cljc:320-322` relies on), then the batch `(stream/next! c)` **marked `:tail? true` at the root**, `c` resolving through the store; no application precedes the call, so `K` is empty (any `let1` or wrapper would push a frame, §5.2 above) | append `\"B\"` | tail, `:next` | halts with `\"B\"` (4b: a tail effect with no frame to pop halts, `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:205-211` stage 2; stack: the seam's empty-`K` case, §4.3), env free of `store-of` | yes |\n| 21 | **free-env shadowing** (the review's row) | initial free env `{x 99}`; `(let1 f (fn [] x) ((fn [x] (f (next-of c))) 1))` | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`; `E` at the read binds `x` to 1; root `free-env` carries `x 99` | the lowered `f` returns `99` (not nil, not 1) on every lane; **the one row the earlier design would have failed** | yes |\n| 22 | nil-valued live register | `(let1 pair (fn [p q] (cat (cat [] p) q)) (pair nil (next-of c)))`: the `nil` operand is evaluated **before** the read and is live across it (`(cat nil (next-of c))` would give `(conj nil \"B\")`, the list `(\"B\")`, so a vector-building `pair` is used; there is no `vector` primitive, `vm.cljc:380-410`, and `pair` builds through the segment's `cat`) | append `\"B\"` | act, `:next`; `W` has a present key with `[:lit nil]` | `[nil \"B\"]` | yes |\n| 23 | tail FFI bookkeeping | a `tail` parked record under a call id `P ∈ :ffi-call-ids` | — | parked, context `:parked`, bookkeeping clause of P4 | validator accepts; the **same valid tail under a key not in `:ffi-call-ids`** is `:parked-site` (P4); moving `site` to a non-tail call is `:site` (T1, which runs first) | **synthetic**: no primitive returns an FFI effect through a tail `:call` today (evaluator §1.6) |\n| 24 | `act` FFI bookkeeping | 3's parked bookkeeping record under its call id | — | parked, P4 bookkeeping | validator accepts | 4b stage 2 |\n\nRefusal rows: `:yin.k/not-quiescent` (`a-nonempty-ready-queue-is-not-quiescent`,\n`:591-603`); `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` (a register kernel stepped one\ninstruction past a `:const`, asked to lift); `:yin.k/non-portable\n:reason-mismatch` (the `:observe` hold, `:675-692`); and the validator's\n**membership tampers**, each a row-set edit of a valid body before\nlower: a window with an extra live key → `:window-extra`; a live key\n303:(defn- bytes-hex\n778:    (wire/byte-payload? x) (hash (bytes-hex x))\n842:(defn numeric-kind\n864:  (case (numeric-kind x)\n895:    (wire/byte-payload? x) [::bytes (bytes-hex x)]\n1039:   built. Returns [[key-bytes-hex key-wire value-wire] ...].\"\n1044:                        [(bytes-hex (wire/encode kw)) kw vw]))\n1176:      :else (let [c (compare (bytes-hex ea) (bytes-hex eb))]\n1450:        (float64-from-bits (bytes-hex b))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc <<'EOF'\n(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.frame\n  \\\"Pure, ordered validation of decoded canonical continuation frames (§3).\\\"\n  (:require [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]))\n\n\n(defn- problem [kind path]\n  {:yin.k/kind kind :yin.k/path path})\n\n\n(defn- closed? [x required optional]\n  (and (map? x) (every? #(contains? x %) required)\n       (every? (into (set required) optional) (keys x))))\n\n\n(defn task-defect\n  \\\"X1, once per body, including a halted body with no frames.\\\"\n  [task]\n  (let [e (:free-env task)]\n    (cond\n      (not (and (map? e) (every? symbol? (keys e))))\n      (problem :free-env-shape [:free-env])\n      (some vm/reserved-name? (keys e))\n      (problem :reserved-name [:free-env]))))\n\n\n(defn- env? [e]\n  (and (closed? e [:yin.k/bindings] [:yin.k/store-of])\n       (map? (:yin.k/bindings e))\n       (every? symbol? (keys (:yin.k/bindings e)))))\n\n\n(defn- lexical-names [v pc]\n  (let [bs (code/body-ranges v)]\n    (loop [b (code/body-index bs pc) names #{}]\n      (if-let [owner (:owner (nth bs b))]\n        (recur (code/body-index bs owner) (into names (nth (nth v owner) 2)))\n        names))))\n\n\n(defn- window-defect [f v rd prefix path]\n  (let [pc (:yin.k/pc f) w (:yin.k/window f)\n        body (nth (code/parse v) (code/body-index (code/body-ranges v) pc))\n        wanted (analysis/saved (analysis/analyze v) pc rd)\n        ks (set (keys w))\n        kind (fn [s] (keyword (str prefix s)))\n        p (conj path :yin.k/window)]\n    (cond\n      (some #(>= % (:registers body)) ks) (problem (kind \\\"window-scope\\\") p)\n      (contains? w rd) (problem (kind \\\"window-self\\\") p)\n      (some #(not (contains? wanted %)) ks) (problem (kind \\\"window-extra\\\") p)\n      (some #(not (contains? w %)) wanted) (problem (kind \\\"window-missing\\\") p))))\n\n\n(defn defect\n  \\\"First §3 defect, or nil. Code is already well formed; task is plain\n   {:free-env map :parked-key P :ffi-call-ids set}. No engine is read.\n   Values have already passed the carrier's value-domain checks.\\\"\n  [frame code-map context task]\n  (let [act? (= :act (:yin.k/state frame))\n        required (if act?\n                   [:yin.k/state :yin.k/segment :yin.k/pc :yin.k/env\n                    :yin.k/window :yin.k/deliver :yin.k/k]\n                   [:yin.k/state :yin.k/segment :yin.k/site :yin.k/deliver :yin.k/k])\n        k (:yin.k/k frame)\n        returns (when (vector? k) (mapv (fn [i] [(nth k i) [:yin.k/k i]]) (range (count k))))\n        all (into [[frame []]] returns)\n        envs (if act? all returns)]\n    (or\n      ;; S1-S4, globally before any dependent read.\n      (when-not (and (contains? #{:act :tail} (:yin.k/state frame))\n                    (closed? frame required [:yin.k/pending]))\n        (problem :frame-shape []))\n      (when-not (vector? k) (problem :k-shape [:yin.k/k]))\n      (some (fn [[f p]]\n              (when-not (and (closed? f [:yin.k/frame-type :yin.k/segment :yin.k/pc\n                                        :yin.k/env :yin.k/window :yin.k/rd] [])\n                             (= :return (:yin.k/frame-type f)))\n                (problem :k-shape p))) returns)\n      (some (fn [[f p]]\n              (when-not (and (map? (:yin.k/window f))\n                             (every? code/reg? (keys (:yin.k/window f))))\n                (problem :window-representation (conj p :yin.k/window)))) envs)\n      (some (fn [[f p]] (when-not (env? (:yin.k/env f))\n                          (problem :env-shape (conj p :yin.k/env)))) envs)\n      (when-not (map? (:yin.k/deliver frame)) (problem :deliver-shape [:yin.k/deliver]))\n      ;; C1-C3 across the entire continuation.\n      (some (fn [[f p]] (when-not (contains? code-map (:yin.k/segment f))\n                          (problem :segment (conj p :yin.k/segment)))) all)\n      (some (fn [[f p]]\n              (let [slot (if (and (empty? p) (not act?)) :yin.k/site :yin.k/pc)\n                    n (get f slot) v (get code-map (:yin.k/segment f))]\n                (cond\n                  (not (code/reg? n)) (problem :pc-kind (conj p slot))\n                  (not (and (< n (count v)) (or (= slot :yin.k/site) (pos? n))))\n                  (problem :pc-bounds (conj p slot))))) all)\n      (some (fn [[f p]]\n              (let [pc (:yin.k/pc f) bs (code/body-ranges (get code-map (:yin.k/segment f)))]\n                (when-not (= (code/body-index bs (dec pc)) (code/body-index bs pc))\n                  (problem :pc-body (conj p :yin.k/pc))))) envs)\n      (let [v (get code-map (:yin.k/segment frame))\n            site (if act? (dec (:yin.k/pc frame)) (:yin.k/site frame))\n            inst (nth v site) op (first inst) rd (code/rd inst)\n            d (:yin.k/deliver frame)]\n        (or\n          (if act?\n            (or\n              (when-not (or (contains? #{:stream-next :stream-put :ffi-call :park :current-continuation} op)\n                            (and (= :call op) (not (code/tail-call? inst))))\n                (problem :site [:yin.k/pc]))\n              (when-not (= rd (:yin.k/rd d)) (problem :destination [:yin.k/deliver :yin.k/rd]))\n              (when-not (= {:yin.k/deliver :rd :yin.k/rd rd} d) (problem :deliver [:yin.k/deliver]))\n              (window-defect frame v rd \\\"\\\" []))\n            (or\n              (when-not (code/tail-call? inst) (problem :site [:yin.k/site]))\n              (when-not (= {:yin.k/deliver :return} d) (problem :deliver [:yin.k/deliver]))))\n          (some (fn [[f p]]\n                  (let [fv (get code-map (:yin.k/segment f)) fi (nth fv (dec (:yin.k/pc f)))\n                        frd (:yin.k/rd f)]\n                    (or\n                      (when-not (and (= :call (first fi)) (not (code/tail-call? fi)))\n                        (problem :return-site (conj p :yin.k/pc)))\n                      (when-not (= frd (code/rd fi)) (problem :return-destination (conj p :yin.k/rd)))\n                      (window-defect f fv frd \\\"return-\\\" p)))) returns)\n          (some (fn [[f p]]\n                  (when (some vm/reserved-name? (keys (get-in f [:yin.k/env :yin.k/bindings])))\n                    (problem :reserved-name (conj p :yin.k/env :yin.k/bindings)))) envs)\n          (some (fn [[f p]]\n                  (let [names (lexical-names (get code-map (:yin.k/segment f)) (:yin.k/pc f))\n                        bindings (get-in f [:yin.k/env :yin.k/bindings])]\n                    (when-not (and (every? #(contains? bindings %) names)\n                                   (= (apply dissoc bindings names)\n                                      (apply dissoc (:free-env task) names)))\n                      (problem :free-env-mismatch (conj p :yin.k/env :yin.k/bindings))))) envs)\n          (when-not (and (contains? #{:wait :captured :parked} context)\n                        (= (= :wait context) (contains? frame :yin.k/pending)))\n            (problem :pending-presence [:yin.k/pending]))\n          (when (= :wait context)\n            (let [reasons (case op\n                            :stream-next #{:next}\n                            :stream-put #{:put}\n                            :ffi-call #{:ffi :ffi-request}\n                            :call #{:next :put :ffi :ffi-request :link-request :link-response :install}\n                            #{})]\n              (when-not (contains? reasons (get-in frame [:yin.k/pending :yin.k/reason]))\n                (problem :reason-mismatch [:yin.k/pending :yin.k/reason]))))\n          (when (and (= :captured context) (not (and act? (= :current-continuation op))))\n            (problem :captured-site [(if act? :yin.k/pc :yin.k/site)]))\n          (when (and (= :parked context)\n                     (not (or (and act? (= :park op))\n                              (and (contains? (:ffi-call-ids task) (:parked-key task))\n                                   (or (and act? (= :ffi-call op))\n                                       (and (not act?) (code/tail-call? inst)))))))\n            (problem :parked-site [(if act? :yin.k/pc :yin.k/site)])))))))\nEOF\nclojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis-test\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
